# The terms the owner keeps off the site. Read by `npm run measure`,
# deliberately never committed — CLAUDE.md says why.
.privacy-terms

# OpenWolf — per-project memory and the hooks that feed it. All of it stays on
# the machine that ran `openwolf init`, never in this repository:
#
#   .wolf/                  session handoff, bug log, anatomy index. Session
#                           memory is exactly where a personal name or address
#                           lands without anyone deciding to write it, and this
#                           repository is public.
#   .claude/settings.json   the 12 hooks, which hardcode an absolute path under
#                           the owner's home directory — a username that carries
#                           part of a name — and point into .wolf/, so they are
#                           broken on any other checkout regardless.
#   .claude/skills|rules|commands
#                           generated by the same init, and they reference
#                           .wolf/ too.
#
# Re-running `openwolf init --agent claude` regenerates every one of these.
.wolf/
.claude/settings.json
.claude/skills/
.claude/rules/
.claude/commands/
